# mise/declared — tools that `dot_config/mise/config.toml` declares itself.
#
# The generated fragments skip these so a tool is never declared twice: mise
# merges `[tools]` per tool and the higher-precedence file wins (config.toml
# beats conf.d/*), so a duplicate would only confuse `mise ls`. Add a name here
# when you move it out of the list files into the hand-maintained config.
#
# node/rust/python are the runtimes `depends` points at, and must stay eager:
# a lazy tool's dependency is never installed for you (mise errors instead).
node
rust
python
speedtest-tui
cline
micromamba
